+# `wipemark/planes` — what this branch carries over upstream
+
+This is `etemesi254/zune-image`'s `zune-jpeg` **0.5.15** with one addition:
+a public `JpegDecoder::decode_planes`, which hands out a JPEG's components
+at their own resolution — the IDCT's output, before upsampling and colour
+conversion — and its quantisation tables. Wipemark
+(`GigLaboCom/wipemark-app`) needs them to restore a visible mark at the
+chroma's own resolution (its decisions D301 and D302; its
+`docs/architecture/zune-jpeg-pin.md`). Nothing that `decode`,
+`decode_into` or any other existing call returns changes.
+
+## Base
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| crate | `zune-jpeg` 0.5.15, as published on crates.io (`checksum 27bc9d5b…7296`) |
+| upstream commit | `31d81fed7551c8ccea456d9d8e2b1fd8bebb6995` (the `.cargo_vcs_info.json` the published crate carries), `crates/zune-jpeg` |
+| this branch's first commit | the published crate's files, unchanged — `Cargo.toml` is crates.io's normalised manifest (`zune-core` from the registry, no `zune-ppm` dev-dependency), `Cargo.toml.orig` is upstream's, so the crate builds on its own |
+| this branch's second commit | the patch below |
+
+The local checkout this was made in could not clone upstream (a container
+without access to GitHub), so the first commit is the crate's published
+source rather than upstream's history. When the fork is created from
+upstream, the patch is applied to `crates/zune-jpeg` at the
+`zune-jpeg-0.5.15` tag (or `31d81fe`): it touches nothing outside
+`crates/zune-jpeg/src`.
+
+## What the patch adds — the public surface
+
+One new file, `src/planes.rs`, re-exported from `lib.rs`:
+
+```rust
+pub struct JpegPlanes {
+    pub width: usize, pub height: usize,
+    pub components: Vec<PlaneOut>,          // frame order: Y, Cb, Cr (or Y alone)
+    pub qt: [Option<[u16; 64]>; 4],         // by slot, NATURAL (row-major) order
+    pub restart_interval: u16,
+    pub progressive: bool,
+}
+pub struct PlaneOut {
+    pub id: u8, pub h: u8, pub v: u8,       // sampling factors
+    pub qt_index: u8,                       // which slot of `qt`
+    pub width: usize, pub height: usize,    // ceil(W·h/h_max) × ceil(H·v/v_max)
+    pub samples: Vec<u8>,                   // row-major, the IDCT's clamped output
+}
+impl<T: ZByteReaderTrait> JpegDecoder<T> {
+    pub fn decode_planes(&mut self) -> Result<JpegPlanes, DecodeErrors>;
+}
+```
+
+Nothing else was made public: no field, function or module of upstream's
+changed visibility.
+
+## Every function touched
+
+| file | function / item | change |
+|---|---|---|
+| `src/lib.rs` | module list, re-exports | `mod planes;`, `pub use crate::planes::{JpegPlanes, PlaneOut};` |
+| `src/decoder.rs` | `JpegDecoder` | two `pub(crate)` fields: `want_planes: bool`, `planes: Vec<PlaneBuf>` |
+| `src/decoder.rs` | `JpegDecoder::default` | initialises them (`false`, empty) |
+| `src/mcu.rs` | `post_process` | first statement: when `want_planes`, `return self.copy_planes(i)` |
+| `src/mcu.rs` | `decode_mcu_ycbcr_baseline` | a component is `needed` (decoded rather than discarded) also when `want_planes`; the YCbCr→Luma `coeff = 2` adjustment does not apply when `want_planes` |
+| `src/mcu.rs` | `finish_baseline_decoding` | `needed` also when `want_planes` |
+| `src/mcu_prog.rs` | `decode_mcu_ycbcr_progressive` | the `coeff = 2` adjustment does not apply when `want_planes` |
+| `src/mcu_prog.rs` | `finish_progressive_decoding` | `needed` also when `want_planes` |
+| `src/planes.rs` (new) | `JpegPlanes`, `PlaneOut`, `decode_planes`; `pub(crate)` `PlaneBuf`, `copy_planes` | the whole addition |
+
+`want_planes` is set only inside `decode_planes`, and cleared before it
+returns, so every other caller runs upstream's code path unchanged — the
+extra conditions are `|| false` and `&& true` for them.
+
+## How it works
+
+* **`decode_planes`** decodes the headers, reads `qt_tables` back (they are
+  stored un-zigzagged, i.e. in natural order, by `parse_dqt`; each value is
+  checked to fit in `u16`, which a 16-bit DQT always does), sets
+  `want_planes`, and runs the decoder's own `decode_mcu_ycbcr_baseline` or
+  `decode_mcu_ycbcr_progressive` with an empty pixel buffer. The tables are
+  the ones defined before the first scan — the ones
+  `setup_component_params` hands the components; a DQT between later scans
+  is not applied by the decoder either.
+* **How upsampling is skipped.** Every path — baseline interleaved, baseline
+  with one scan per component, progressive — ends each row of MCUs in
+  `post_process`, which upsamples (`worker::upsample`) and converts
+  (`worker::color_convert`). With `want_planes` on, `post_process` instead
+  calls `copy_planes(i)` and returns before either: no upsampler and no
+  colour converter runs, and the pixel buffer is never touched.
+* **How the padding is cropped.** `copy_planes` allocates each plane on the
+  first row of MCUs at `ceil(width · h / h_max) × ceil(height · v /
+  v_max)` — `h_max`/`v_max` as `setup_component_params` (and, for a grey
+  picture with sampling factors, `reset_params`) left them — filled with
+  128, the value `decode` fills rows a damaged scan never reached with.
+  Row of MCUs `i` of a component is its `raw_coeff`: `8 · v` rows of
+  `width_stride` samples (the IDCT's output, clamped to 0–255 by the IDCT
+  itself). Row `r` lands at plane row `i · 8v + r` when that is below the
+  plane's height, and only its first `width` samples are copied: the
+  columns and rows the MCU grid adds past the picture are dropped.
+* **Arithmetic coding** stays refused, as upstream refuses it (`SOF9`–`SOF15`
+  are refused when the frame header is read, before any of this runs).
+* **No coefficients.** The quantised DCT coefficients are not exported.
+
+## Size
+
+The patch commit touches 5 source files and adds this one: `src/planes.rs` new (196
+lines, of which ~80 are documentation), 21 lines added across the four
+existing files, none removed.
+
+## Tests
+
+The crate's own suite (`cargo test`, 22 tests: unit tests and doctests)
+passes unchanged. The patch's tests live in Wipemark, which has the
+fixtures: `crates/wipemark-picture/tests/planes.rs` holds the planes,
+upsampled by an independent restatement of this crate's scalar upsampler
+and colour conversion, to `decode`'s RGB output byte for byte (4:4:4,
+4:2:2, 4:2:0, grey, progressive, restart intervals, one- and two-segment
+DQT, a 16-bit table), the 4:2:0 chroma at quality 100 to the 2 × 2 means of
+the picture it was encoded from, and `qt` to the tables read from the DQT
+segments by a marker walk of its own. `cargo clippy` reports the same 105
+warnings with the patch as without it (none in `planes.rs`).
+
+## Re-carrying onto a new tag
+
+1. Branch from the new `zune-jpeg-<version>` tag (never merge histories).
+2. `git cherry-pick` the patch commit. The touched spots are small and
+   named in the table above; on a conflict, re-apply them by hand:
+   the two fields and their initialisers, the early return at the top of
+   `post_process`, `|| self.want_planes` in the three `needed` conditions,
+   `&& !self.want_planes` in the two `coeff = 2` conditions.
+3. Check what the new version changed around them: that every decoding
+   path still ends each row of MCUs in `post_process`; that `raw_coeff` is
+   still `8 · v` rows of `width_stride` IDCT output; that `qt_tables` is
+   still stored in natural order; that `post_process` still upsamples and
+   converts (and nothing before it does).
+4. Update this file's base table, run this crate's tests and Wipemark's
+   (`cargo test -p wipemark-picture --test planes`, and the pinned-hash
+   test `the_rgb_raster_did_not_move`, which moves only when upstream's own
+   output moved — then it is re-pinned with the reason written down), and
+   pin the new commit in Wipemark's root `Cargo.toml`.
